The section lists the student's items, oldest first, and downloads their
files.
The list says what each item is and when it came, which matters when there
are several; the files follow it, converted by [[canvaslms]].

<<functions>>=
def work_section(activity, users, workdir):
    """Return the `Section` of the work that `users` handed in."""
    items = sorted((item for item in activity.submissions
                    if related_id(item, "user") in users),
                   key=lambda item: attribute(item, "created-at"))
    if not items:
        return Section(WORK_TITLE, "Nothing handed in.")
    base = media_base(activity.fbf.login.api_url)
    lines, files = [], []
    for item in items:
        media = related_id(item, "media")
        path = media and download_media(activity.fbf.session, base, media,
                                        workdir)
        line = (f"- {attribute(item, 'title')} "
                f"({attribute(item, 'category')}, "
                f"{attribute(item, 'created-at')})")
        lines.append(line if path else f"{line}: {NO_FILE}")
        if path:
            files.append(path)
    return Section(WORK_TITLE, "\n".join(lines), files)
@


\section{The grade}
\label{ViewGrade}

The grade breakdown is that of [[fbf progress]] (\cref{Progress}) for one
student.
We cannot call [[assignment_progress]], which builds the rows of all
students, fetches the Canvas scores of all and reports on all of them on
standard error; we take its parts instead.
Of the student's progresses we take the one that explains the grade, by
the same [[preference]], and the grade sent is fetched for that one only.
The Canvas score is the submission's own, which [[canvaslms]] already has.

<<constants>>=
GRADE_TITLE = "FeedbackFruits grade"
<<functions>>=
def grade_section(activity, users, assignment, student, score):
    """Return the `Section` of the grade breakdown of `users`."""
    mine = [progress for progress in activity.progresses
            if related_id(progress, "actor") in users]
    if not mine:
        return Section(GRADE_TITLE, "No progress in FeedbackFruits.")
    progress = max(mine, key=progress_module.preference)
    row = progress_module.progress_row(
        assignment, progress, activity.tasks,
        progress_module.sent_grades(activity.fbf, [progress]),
        student, {student.id: score})
    return Section(GRADE_TITLE, grade_text(row))
@

The text gives the totals first and then the facets, the parts that FBF
adds up to the total, with the points earned of the points possible.
FBF's overall grade is a percentage (\cref{Progress}); we show it beside
the score in Canvas's points, since the two may differ and the difference
is what a teacher looks for.

<<functions>>=
def grade_text(row):
    """Return the Markdown of a `Progress` row."""
    number = progress_module.number
    lines = [f"- Overall: {number(row.overall)} %, "
             f"{number(row.fbf_score)} of {number(row.points_possible)} "
             "points",
             f"- In Canvas: {number(row.canvas_score)} points",
             f"- Published by FeedbackFruits: "
             f"{'yes' if row.published else 'no'}"]
    if row.sent_grade is not None:
        lines.append(f"- Sent to Canvas: {row.sent_grade} ({row.sent_status})")
    facets = [f"- {facet.task_type} {facet.task_order}: "
              f"{progress_module.facet_text(facet)}"
              for facet in row.facets if facet.weight]
    return "\n".join(lines + ([""] + facets if facets else []))
@


\section{The reviews}
\label{ViewReviews}

A student both receives reviews and gives them, and a teacher needs both:
the reviews received explain much of the student's own grade, the reviews
given are often part of it.
Both come from the allocations of the review task, the student being the
[[allocable]] in one case and the [[actor]] in the other.
The fetchers of \cref{Reviews} take a test of the allocations to keep, so
we pass one for each and pay only for the student's allocations, a handful
of requests instead of hundreds.
With the reviews come the ratings of them: those the student gave the
reviews received, and those the reviewees gave the student's reviews.

<<constants>>=
RECEIVED_TITLE = "Reviews received"
GIVEN_TITLE = "Reviews given"
<<imports>>=
from fbf import reviews as review_module
<<functions>>=
def review_sections(activity, users):
    """Return the `Section`s of the reviews that `users` got and gave."""
    sections = []
    for title, role, other in [(RECEIVED_TITLE, "allocable", "reviewer"),
                               (GIVEN_TITLE, "actor", "reviewee")]:
        keep = in_role(users, role)
        reviews = review_module.fetch_reviews(activity.fbf, activity.task,
                                              "", keep=keep)
        feedbacks = review_module.fetch_feedback(activity.fbf, activity.task,
                                                 "", keep=keep)
        sections.append(Section(title, reviews_text(reviews, feedbacks,
                                                    other)))
    return sections


def in_role(users, role):
    """Return a test of whether an allocation has one of `users` as `role`."""
    return lambda allocation: review_module.person(allocation, role) in users
@

The text groups everything by the other party, the reviewer of a review
received or the reviewee of a review given, since that is how a review
reads: one person's assessment, criterion by criterion, then the rating it
got.
The comments are folded onto one line each, as in the [[fbf reviews]]
output, so that the list stays a list.

<<functions>>=
def reviews_text(reviews, feedbacks, other):
    """Return the Markdown of `reviews` and `feedbacks`, by `other` party."""
    parties = list(dict.fromkeys(
        [getattr(review, other) for review in reviews]
        + [getattr(feedback, other) for feedback in feedbacks]))
    if not parties:
        return "None."
    lines = []
    for party in parties:
        lines.append(f"- {party or 'Unknown'}")
        for review in reviews:
            if getattr(review, other) == party:
                level = f": {review.level} ({review.score})" \
                    if review.level else ""
                lines.append(f"  - {review.criterion}{level}")
                lines += [f"    - {review_module.fold(comment.body)}"
                          for comment in review.comments]
        for feedback in feedbacks:
            if getattr(feedback, other) == party:
                body = review_module.fold(feedback.body)
                lines.append(f"  - Rating of the review: {feedback.rating}"
                             + (f", {body}" if body else ""))
    return "\n".join(lines)
