\section{Putting it together}
\label{ViewTogether}

Which parts an activity has depends on its tasks: a peer review has a
submit task, a review task and perhaps a reflect task; a video activity
has a multimedia task; every activity has a grade.
We show the parts that the tasks call for, in the order a teacher reads
them: what was handed in, what it earned, what others said about it, what
the student said about others, and the student's own words.

A part that fails costs only itself.
One may fail where another does not: a group peer review, which we cannot
read (\cref{Reviews}), still has a grade.
So the error goes in the part's place, as text, and the other parts are
still shown.
The steps before the parts, the launch and finding the student, have no
such fallback: without them there is nothing to show, and the error goes
to [[canvaslms]], which reports it and shows the Canvas part.

<<viewer methods>>=
def sections(self, submission, workdir):
    """Return the `Section`s of the FBF work behind a Canvas `submission`.

    `submission.assignment` must be its assignment.  Returns `[]` when that
    is not an FBF assignment.  Files are downloaded into `workdir`.  Raises
    one of `ERRORS` when FBF cannot be reached.
    """
    assignment = submission.assignment
    code = fbfcanvas.placement_code(assignment)
    if code is None:
        return []
    fbf, activities = self.course(assignment.course_id)
    if code not in activities:
        return [Section(WORK_TITLE, NOT_OPENED)]
    activity = self.activity(fbf, activities[code])
    student = self.student(assignment.course_id, submission.user_id)
    if student is None:
        return [Section(WORK_TITLE, NOT_A_STUDENT)]
    users = student_users(fbf, activity.users, student, self.emails)
    if not users:
        return [Section(WORK_TITLE, NOT_TAKEN_PART)]
    return each_part(<<the parts of [[activity]]>>)
@

Each part is a title, for the error message, and a function giving its
sections, guarded by whether the activity has the task.

<<the parts of [[activity]]>>=
[(WORK_TITLE, SUBMIT_TASK in activity.task,
  lambda: [work_section(activity, users, workdir)]),
 (GRADE_TITLE, True,
  lambda: [grade_section(activity, users, assignment, student,
                         submission.score)]),
 (RECEIVED_TITLE, review_module.REVIEW_TASK in activity.task,
  lambda: review_sections(activity, users)),
 (REFLECTION_TITLE, review_module.REFLECT_TASK in activity.task,
  lambda: [reflection_section(activity, users)]),
 (DISCUSSION_TITLE, MULTIMEDIA_TASK in activity.task,
  lambda: [discussion_section(activity, users)])]
<<constants>>=
FAILED = "Could not fetch this from FeedbackFruits: {}"
<<functions>>=
def each_part(parts):
    """Return the sections of the `parts` that apply, errors in place."""
    sections = []
    for title, applies, build in parts:
        if not applies:
            continue
        try:
            sections += build()
        except ERRORS as error:
            sections.append(Section(title, FAILED.format(error)))
    return sections
@

<<test functions>>=
def test_each_part_puts_an_error_in_the_parts_place():
  def broken():
    raise APIError(500, "GET", "https://api.example/v1/x")
  def buggy():
    raise TypeError("bug")
  sections = each_part([("A", True, lambda: [Section("A", "a")]),
                        ("B", True, broken),
                        ("C", False, buggy)])
  assert [(s.title, s.body) for s in sections] == [
    ("A", "a"), ("B", FAILED.format("GET /v1/x: HTTP 500"))]
  with pytest.raises(TypeError):
    each_part([("C", True, buggy)])
@

